WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.190
Sometimes you cannot measure things one at a time.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.210
You only know totals of pairs.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.520
The useful trick is to add all the measurements and ask

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.050
how many times each unknown has been counted.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.030
This replaces trial and error with one clean step.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.060
Instead of guessing the three values, you find their

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.430
total first, and everything else follows by subtraction.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.120
Three boxes are weighed in pairs.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.380
The first and second weigh ten kilograms together.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.540
The second and third weigh fourteen.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.760
The first and third weigh twelve.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:33.880
How heavy is each box?

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.660
Pause and try adding all three readings.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.580
Add the three readings: ten plus fourteen plus

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.690
twelve is thirty-six.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.390
Look at the table.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.390
Each box was on the scales exactly twice.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.140
So thirty-six is twice the total weight, and the three

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.470
boxes weigh eighteen kilograms altogether.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:57.060
Now subtract.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.820
The second and third weigh fourteen, so the first weighs

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.610
eighteen minus fourteen, which is four.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.420
In the same way the second weighs six and the

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.530
third weighs eight.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.710
Check every reading.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:11.570
Four and six make ten.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.650
Six and eight make fourteen.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.750
Four and eight make twelve.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.220
Watch for unequal counting.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.560
In a triangle puzzle where each side has a total,

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.710
the corner numbers lie on two sides, but the middle

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.520
numbers lie on only one.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.630
Adding the three side totals counts corners twice

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.780
and middles once.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.300
You must keep track of that difference, not ignore it.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.090
Add the measurements.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.410
Count how often each unknown appears.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.650
Then subtract to separate them.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.940
Notebook challenge: three numbers are added in pairs to

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.150
give seventeen, twenty and twenty-three.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.930
What are the three numbers?
